WEBVTT

00:02.318 --> 00:05.253
Check it out.
They got cars that run on vegetable oil now.

00:05.422 --> 00:07.413
- How about that.
- You know what'd be cool?

00:07.590 --> 00:10.957
- A Hummer that runs on french fry grease.
- Uh-huh.

00:11.127 --> 00:13.652
We could be energy independent
and still smash through crap.

00:14.097 --> 00:15.496
Sounds great.

00:15.665 --> 00:18.634
Plus, the new-car smell is french fries.

00:18.802 --> 00:20.997
Okay, I'm only gonna say this
one more time.

00:21.171 --> 00:24.538
You don't get a license for two more years
and you're not getting a Hummer.

00:24.974 --> 00:28.637
You know, you say you want me
to open up to you, but what's the point?

00:33.583 --> 00:36.518
Yeah, I always loved Paris
in the springtime.

00:36.686 --> 00:39.655
Oh, you're lucky.
I only got to do her once on Halloween.

00:42.692 --> 00:44.592
- Hi.
- Oh, hey, Alan.

00:44.761 --> 00:46.786
- Andy, this is my brother, Alan.
- Alan, Andy.

00:46.963 --> 00:48.555
- Hello.
- Hi, Andy.

00:48.732 --> 00:50.996
- Pull up a chair. We're telling war stories.
- Oh, great.

00:52.435 --> 00:54.494
- The sponge?
- Yeah.

00:56.005 --> 00:57.802
So, uh, how do you guys
know each other?

00:59.442 --> 01:02.309
- Well, Andy and I-
- Can I have a cigar?

01:04.447 --> 01:06.938
- Uh, sure. Help yourself.
- Oh, thank you.

01:08.151 --> 01:09.880
Anyway, Andy and I have known-

01:10.053 --> 01:12.920
Maybe I'll take one for now
and one for later.

01:17.060 --> 01:18.527
Anyway...

01:18.695 --> 01:21.994
...before he moved to New York,
Andy and I were partners in crime.

01:22.165 --> 01:25.760
- There weren't that many actual crimes.
- Unless you count the ones against nature.

01:27.337 --> 01:30.864
- Alan, this is a great man.
No, no.

01:31.040 --> 01:32.803
Albert Einstein was a great man.

01:32.976 --> 01:35.570
I just drink, gamble and hump.
But I'm great at it.

01:37.514 --> 01:41.211
Andy once managed to hitchhike
from Vegas to L.A. wearing no pants.

01:42.385 --> 01:44.876
Hey, anybody can use their thumb.

01:46.656 --> 01:49.750
This right here,
this is the brother I never had.

01:50.727 --> 01:53.025
Oh, well, how nice for you.

01:54.097 --> 01:56.691
I don't mean it that way.
You're my brother.

01:56.866 --> 01:59.960
- Well, thank you.
- I just like him better.

02:01.271 --> 02:03.739
- Got it.
- Andy is the one guy in the world...

02:03.907 --> 02:06.467
...who can match me drink for drink
and broad for broad.

02:06.643 --> 02:10.545
One time I thought I drank him under
the table, he had a broad under there.

02:10.713 --> 02:13.273
Heh-heh-heh. Right, Andy?

02:15.418 --> 02:16.908
Andy?

02:18.555 --> 02:20.682
Don't screw with me, dude.

02:26.162 --> 02:27.891
Who's your favorite brother now?

02:42.378 --> 02:44.642
So he died out there in the chair, huh?

02:44.814 --> 02:46.076
Yep.

02:46.850 --> 02:49.478
Remind me to flip that cushion.

02:50.787 --> 02:54.154
You should've seen it. The paramedics
zipped him up in a big plastic bag.

02:54.324 --> 02:56.315
- Is that so?
- It looked like those things...

02:56.492 --> 02:59.120
...the delivery guys use to keep pizza hot.

02:59.896 --> 03:02.865
I wonder if they got him to the morgue
in 30 minutes or less.

03:05.368 --> 03:06.528
Not funny, Jake.

03:07.170 --> 03:09.365
Maybe it is funny
and you just didn't get it.

03:10.506 --> 03:11.996
Eat.

03:12.642 --> 03:13.836
So, uh, did you know him?

03:14.277 --> 03:16.074
Andy? Sure.

03:16.246 --> 03:19.147
Before he moved to New York,
he and Charlie were like brothers.

03:19.315 --> 03:20.976
Yeah, I heard that part.

03:21.417 --> 03:23.544
- How's Charlie taking it?
- He's pretty shook up.

03:23.720 --> 03:26.120
Well, you can understand why.

03:26.556 --> 03:27.784
Somebody your age...

03:27.957 --> 03:30.221
...living the same dumb-ass lifestyle
you lived...

03:31.361 --> 03:33.989
...keels over and dies?
It's gotta give you pause.

03:35.531 --> 03:38.523
- You're right about that.
- I'm surprised Charlie didn't go first.

03:38.701 --> 03:40.464
Excuse me.

03:42.205 --> 03:43.672
I'm standing right here.

03:44.040 --> 03:46.133
But for how long?

03:48.645 --> 03:49.839
Did you get that one?

03:51.781 --> 03:53.646
- See you later.
- Uh, where you going?

03:53.816 --> 03:54.840
Where do you think?

03:55.018 --> 03:57.543
My best friend just died,
I got a lot to take care of.

03:57.720 --> 04:00.518
You're handling the funeral?
I'm sure Andy would like that.

04:00.690 --> 04:04.558
To hell with Andy, I'm going to the hospital
to get every test known to man.

04:05.962 --> 04:07.293
Good one.

04:08.498 --> 04:10.398
You're not getting any of these, are you?

04:16.372 --> 04:18.897
- Hey.
- Hey. How'd the tests go?

04:19.309 --> 04:20.901
I won't know for a couple of days.

04:21.077 --> 04:24.012
All right, I'm out of here.

04:24.180 --> 04:25.408
How about you, Charlie?

04:30.420 --> 04:33.082
Wait, I got something for you.

04:33.256 --> 04:36.350
It's a gift certificate for a week at a spa
in Palm Springs.

04:36.526 --> 04:39.393
Well, I'll be. Thank you, Charlie.

04:39.829 --> 04:42.263
I just wanted you to know
that I love you...

04:42.432 --> 04:45.026
...and appreciate
that you've always been there for me.

04:45.201 --> 04:46.600
Great, see you in a week.

04:51.341 --> 04:54.071
The minute you start thinking
about your mortality...

04:54.243 --> 04:57.076
...you realize how much you care
about the people around you.

04:57.246 --> 04:59.043
Yeah, and I need to start showing it.

04:59.215 --> 05:00.739
Well...

05:00.917 --> 05:04.409
...little gifts are always a nice way
to express your feelings.

05:05.088 --> 05:06.487
I know.

05:06.656 --> 05:09.489
Could be as simple as a cashmere robe...

05:09.926 --> 05:14.226
...or, uh, as extravagant as a new car.

05:14.397 --> 05:16.558
- Yeah, I suppose it could. Ahem.
- Yeah.

05:17.300 --> 05:20.667
Excuse me,
I got something really cool for Jake.

05:22.138 --> 05:24.003
Doesn't even have to be new.

05:24.440 --> 05:27.705
Certified pre-owned
is still very thoughtful.

05:31.547 --> 05:34.482
- Hey, what are you doing?
- I was trying to research cars...

05:34.650 --> 05:37.710
...but you wouldn't believe what comes
up when you Google "Hummer."

05:40.690 --> 05:42.089
Actually, I would.

05:44.460 --> 05:47.657
Here, I got you something
I think you're really gonna like.

05:47.830 --> 05:49.127
Is it a sandwich?

05:49.866 --> 05:51.493
Why would I giftwrap a sandwich?

05:51.667 --> 05:53.692
Because you want me to be surprised?

05:53.870 --> 05:55.565
Just open it.

05:55.972 --> 05:58.964
You know what's a great sandwich?
The Monte Cristo.

05:59.142 --> 06:02.543
Because it has ham and cheese,
and it's fried.

06:02.979 --> 06:04.207
Open the damn box.

06:04.380 --> 06:07.110
Whoa, don't get your period.

06:09.652 --> 06:12.314
- Oh, wow, a mini video-camera.
- Pretty cool, huh?

06:12.488 --> 06:14.479
Is this because you think you're dying?

06:14.657 --> 06:17.854
No, no. I just wanted
to do something nice for you.

06:18.027 --> 06:19.187
Before you die.

06:19.829 --> 06:22.320
- Do you want the camera or not?
- Yeah, I want it.

06:22.498 --> 06:24.398
- Then just say thank you.
- Thank you.

06:24.567 --> 06:27.365
Jeez, you need to relax.
You'll give yourself a heart attack.

06:29.105 --> 06:30.629
I'll work on it.

06:30.807 --> 06:33.708
Have a sandwich.
That always relaxes me.

06:36.179 --> 06:38.739
All right, one more gift to give.

06:39.515 --> 06:42.382
Oh, yeah? Saving the best for last?

06:44.487 --> 06:47.684
I don't know about the best,
but it's sure the hardest.

06:48.257 --> 06:50.088
Any way I can make it easier?

06:50.259 --> 06:51.749
Yeah.

06:52.028 --> 06:54.826
Call Mom
and tell her I'm on my way over.

07:01.104 --> 07:05.268
Oh, Charlie, what a beautiful watch.

07:05.808 --> 07:10.040
- Do you really like it?
- Are you kidding? It's gorgeous.

07:10.213 --> 07:13.614
And the best part is now I don't
have to wear my good one every day.

07:17.120 --> 07:19.611
You're probably wondering
why I bought it for you.

07:20.156 --> 07:22.249
Well, I just assumed you love me...

07:22.425 --> 07:24.620
...and did it out of the goodness
of your heart.

07:25.828 --> 07:28.388
Kidding. Why, dear?

07:28.564 --> 07:29.929
Okay, I deserve that.

07:31.300 --> 07:33.200
But the truth is I do love you...

07:33.369 --> 07:36.304
...and despite our many differences,
I'm glad you're my mother.

07:37.406 --> 07:39.533
You didn't drive over here drunk, did you?

07:42.011 --> 07:44.946
I'm not drunk. I just, uh...

07:45.515 --> 07:48.643
I've been thinking a lot
about how fleeting life is...

07:48.818 --> 07:51.719
...that none of us really knows
how long we're gonna be here.

07:52.155 --> 07:55.056
Did you find another lump
on your pee-pee?

07:57.460 --> 07:59.553
No, Mom, my pee-pee's fine.

08:00.263 --> 08:04.290
I don't know how "worn down to a nub"
can be fine, but all right.

08:06.102 --> 08:09.503
My point is, uh, I don't wanna be angry
with you anymore.

08:09.672 --> 08:11.003
I want us to be friends.

08:11.440 --> 08:15.035
I was always your friend, Charlie.

08:15.211 --> 08:17.645
You were just too self-involved to see it.

08:21.484 --> 08:23.179
Okay, I gotta go.

08:23.953 --> 08:25.352
Where you off to?

08:25.521 --> 08:28.081
I have to pick out a casket
for a friend of mine.

08:28.257 --> 08:30.157
Oh, I'm- I'm so sorry.

08:30.426 --> 08:33.020
Yeah, well, what are you gonna do?

08:33.196 --> 08:34.288
Well, don't cheap out.

08:34.730 --> 08:38.029
It's one thing to do it with a watch,
but a casket is forever.

08:45.675 --> 08:48.735
So young. I can't believe it.

08:48.911 --> 08:50.344
Yeah.

08:50.513 --> 08:54.040
Who would've thought smoking,
drinking and whoring could kill you?

08:55.117 --> 08:58.052
You realize that could just as easily
be me in there.

08:58.221 --> 08:59.984
Yeah.

09:00.590 --> 09:02.455
Don't even think that.

09:03.993 --> 09:05.824
It is a nice casket, though.

09:05.995 --> 09:07.189
Should be.

09:07.363 --> 09:10.093
- It cost me 10 grand.
- Ten grand, wow.

09:10.266 --> 09:13.463
What can I say,
I take care of the people I love.

09:13.636 --> 09:16.503
Could've taken care of me
with a freaking robe.

09:19.141 --> 09:21.109
Kind of a light turnout.

09:21.277 --> 09:23.677
You'd probably get more people
with an open bar.

09:23.846 --> 09:25.837
Hey, make sure
there's an open bar at mine.

09:26.449 --> 09:28.178
Oh, now, I'm your funeral planner?

09:28.351 --> 09:31.980
Don't you want a friend or someone
you really care about in charge of that?

09:32.221 --> 09:33.381
No, you do it.

09:35.157 --> 09:38.149
Good afternoon and welcome.

09:38.327 --> 09:41.524
We are here to celebrate the life...

09:41.697 --> 09:46.498
...and mourn the passing
of Andrew Donald Patterson.

09:46.669 --> 09:49.900
How do we measure a man's life?

09:50.072 --> 09:53.007
- By...
- Jeez, this guy's a load.

09:55.578 --> 09:57.944
Don't get a guy like this for me.

09:58.114 --> 10:01.015
I want someone
with a little bit of gravitas.

10:01.450 --> 10:03.748
I'll see if James Earl Jones is available.

10:03.919 --> 10:05.113
That would be nice.

10:05.288 --> 10:10.225
- Born, a time to die, a time to reap...

10:10.893 --> 10:15.353
...a time to sow, a time to mourn...

10:15.531 --> 10:16.930
A time to heal...

10:17.099 --> 10:19.260
...a time for every purpose under heaven.

10:19.435 --> 10:22.962
And so we say goodbye
to Charles Francis Harper.

10:23.406 --> 10:27.069
Devoted son, loving brother,
caring uncle...

10:27.543 --> 10:32.105
...bon vivant and world-class connoisseur
of the booty.

10:34.050 --> 10:35.381
Nice turnout.

10:35.551 --> 10:39.112
I'd like to take this moment...
- Yeah. Standing room only.

10:39.622 --> 10:42.489
Goes to show you,
give the people what they want.

10:43.259 --> 10:44.817
You mean the open bar, right?

10:45.494 --> 10:46.859
Sure.

10:50.099 --> 10:51.566
Thanks for coming, by the way.

10:51.734 --> 10:52.928
You came to mine.

10:53.235 --> 10:54.896
Yeah, but you're dead.

10:55.371 --> 10:57.601
Charlie, take a look in the box.

10:57.773 --> 10:59.638
That's not a tanning booth.

11:00.343 --> 11:02.072
Oh, yeah.

11:02.845 --> 11:06.008
So listen, as long as you're here,
what's heaven like?

11:06.182 --> 11:08.707
It's unbelievable. It's paradise.

11:08.884 --> 11:11.648
Like your house
before your brother moved in.

11:11.821 --> 11:13.448
Oh, that was good.

11:13.622 --> 11:15.522
You can drink all you want, no hangover.

11:15.925 --> 11:18.826
Endless supply of women,
each one more beautiful than the last.

11:18.994 --> 11:21.986
And Charlie, get this:
They believe everything you tell them.

11:22.965 --> 11:25.900
- Everything?
- It's heaven, dude.

11:27.403 --> 11:28.768
Wow.

11:28.938 --> 11:31.236
- Well, save me a good seat.
- I wish I could...

11:31.407 --> 11:33.136
...but that's not where they sent me.

11:33.309 --> 11:34.867
Ew.

11:35.711 --> 11:38.043
Then how do you know
what heaven's like?

11:38.414 --> 11:41.281
They make us look at a video every day...

11:41.450 --> 11:44.442
...while they're putting lube
on the pitchfork.

11:46.055 --> 11:48.046
Well, at least, you get lube.

11:48.624 --> 11:50.182
Only on the middle prong.

11:52.328 --> 11:53.852
To be completely honest...

11:54.230 --> 11:56.198
...I didn't know Charlie Harper.

11:56.365 --> 12:02.395
But any man, who, with his dying breath,
would set aside $25,000...

12:02.571 --> 12:06.234
...and a first-class air ticket
so I could deliver his eulogy...

12:06.409 --> 12:08.673
...is aces in my book.

12:10.045 --> 12:13.811
That being said, there are many people
here today who did know Charlie...

12:13.983 --> 12:17.043
...and perhaps some would like
to stand up and say a few words.

12:17.219 --> 12:19.710
Ooh, ooh! Ah, I wanna say something.

12:19.889 --> 12:21.117
Uh...

12:21.290 --> 12:22.484
...hello, everybody.

12:23.459 --> 12:25.154
Hello, James Earl Jones.

12:27.763 --> 12:30.095
Um, hey, bro. Don't get up.

12:31.967 --> 12:34.333
Ah, what can I say about Charlie?

12:34.503 --> 12:37.233
Uh, so many words come to mind.

12:37.406 --> 12:38.998
So few that you can say in church.

12:40.543 --> 12:42.010
But we'll, uh- We'll give it a shot.

12:43.379 --> 12:46.746
Um, Charlie was a man of love.

12:46.916 --> 12:48.884
Um, he loved his friends...

12:49.051 --> 12:50.678
...he loved his family...

12:50.853 --> 12:52.081
...but most of all...

12:52.254 --> 12:53.414
...he loved his penis.

12:55.191 --> 12:58.024
The only part of him
that ever had an actual job.

13:00.329 --> 13:02.263
Ah, anyway...

13:02.431 --> 13:07.733
...this was a man, uh, so full of love
that it practically oozed out of him.

13:07.903 --> 13:10.394
Ah, at which point, of course,
he would see a doctor.

13:16.078 --> 13:18.012
But I- I kid the deceased whoremonger.

13:19.882 --> 13:25.912
Anyway, uh, since he never made out a will,
uh, I hope you will all join me...

13:26.088 --> 13:29.922
...for a wake-slash-luau
at my Malibu beach house.

13:34.797 --> 13:36.264
He got my house?

13:36.432 --> 13:38.457
- He got everything you had.
- Everything?

13:38.767 --> 13:42.134
Well, not the diseased liver
and the swollen prostate.

13:43.939 --> 13:47.602
Oh, look. Your old girlfriends
are saying their final goodbye.

13:54.483 --> 13:56.542
That's not very respectful.

13:56.719 --> 14:00.815
Just FYI, spit is the devil's lube.

14:03.192 --> 14:06.753
Listen. Uh, would you mind recording
my answering-machine message for me?

14:07.396 --> 14:08.954
That'll be an extra $500.

14:09.698 --> 14:11.188
That's okay. I'm rich now.

14:11.734 --> 14:15.602
All right, what do you want, uh,
"This is CNN" or "Luke, I am your father"?

14:15.771 --> 14:18.672
So, Charlie, it's been great catching up,
but I gotta go.

14:19.408 --> 14:21.638
Already? Can't you stay a while?

14:22.611 --> 14:26.342
No, it's pitchfork time.
If you're late, you don't get the spit.

14:28.350 --> 14:30.716
And believe me, Charlie,
you want the spit.

14:32.154 --> 14:34.145
I want the spit.

14:48.270 --> 14:52.468
Harper. Charlie Harper.
I was in a few days ago.

14:53.208 --> 14:55.267
I peed in a cup, you took my blood...

14:55.443 --> 14:58.207
...and slipped a camera
up the heart of darkness.

14:59.648 --> 15:03.084
Well, the doctor said my results
would be ready today.

15:03.685 --> 15:05.653
Fine, have him get back to me.

15:07.489 --> 15:09.389
He's avoiding my calls, Alan.

15:09.557 --> 15:12.151
- I'm gonna die.
- No, no, you're not.

15:12.327 --> 15:14.659
Aah. I can feel it.

15:14.829 --> 15:17.764
You might as well just drive into that tree
and kill us both.

15:18.433 --> 15:22.665
Sure. I don't wanna go on living
without you.

15:23.738 --> 15:25.865
What's the point of it all?

15:26.041 --> 15:30.000
Yeah, I'm rich, charming,
classically handsome...

15:30.545 --> 15:33.173
...I've laid more pipe than a guy...

15:33.348 --> 15:35.578
...who has sex with pipes.

15:36.518 --> 15:39.544
But what have I done with my life?

15:39.721 --> 15:44.624
A few stupid jingles, some kids' songs,
nothing that really matters.

15:44.793 --> 15:48.251
Now, now,
you're being too hard on yourself.

15:48.697 --> 15:51.598
Got no wife, I've got no children.

15:51.766 --> 15:53.825
I'm gonna leave this world
the way I came in.

15:54.202 --> 15:56.466
By a cesarean section?

15:57.572 --> 15:59.472
Alone.

15:59.808 --> 16:03.505
Oh, for God's sake, Charlie,
I am tired of listening to this.

16:03.678 --> 16:05.873
There has always been
one person in your life...

16:06.047 --> 16:08.777
...who's been there for you
and loved you unconditionally.

16:11.786 --> 16:13.447
You mean...

16:16.691 --> 16:18.022
You're right.

16:18.193 --> 16:20.218
- How could I have missed it?
- Heh-heh-heh.

16:20.395 --> 16:22.124
It's been in front of me the whole time.

16:22.297 --> 16:24.197
You can't see the forest for the trees...

16:24.366 --> 16:26.926
...even when the forest
is in your own backyard.

16:27.102 --> 16:28.694
Or guest room, heh, heh.

16:30.205 --> 16:31.797
Rose?

16:33.708 --> 16:35.903
- Yup, the one and only.
- Aah.

16:36.077 --> 16:39.205
I know, I know, it's been a while.

16:39.881 --> 16:42.577
If you're not too busy
maybe we could get together...

16:42.751 --> 16:44.844
...and have a drink or something.

16:45.019 --> 16:46.452
Great.

16:46.621 --> 16:48.816
So do you wanna meet
or should I pick you up?

16:54.496 --> 16:56.361
&lt;i>I'll meet you at your place.&lt;/i>

16:57.332 --> 16:59.323
Okay, I'll meet you back at my place.

17:03.538 --> 17:05.335
Small world.

17:05.507 --> 17:08.943
Yeah, teeny-tiny.

17:13.515 --> 17:16.541
- Here you go.
- Thank you, Charlie.

17:16.718 --> 17:18.913
- Comfy?
- Oh, very.

17:19.087 --> 17:20.611
Good.

17:24.426 --> 17:27.953
- So, Rose.
- Charlie.

17:28.596 --> 17:32.088
- Haven't seen you in a while.
- Can't say the same.

17:34.302 --> 17:36.236
Oh, right, right. Sure, yeah.

17:36.404 --> 17:37.894
Sorry about your friend.

17:38.573 --> 17:39.597
Yeah.

17:39.774 --> 17:41.901
Yeah, it was a real wake-up call for me.

17:42.610 --> 17:43.736
I can imagine.

17:45.046 --> 17:48.209
Makes you stop and wonder
what's important in your life.

17:48.383 --> 17:50.783
Who's important in your life.

17:50.952 --> 17:53.386
I've always known
who's important in my life.

17:53.955 --> 17:55.650
You have, haven't you?

17:57.592 --> 17:59.924
You know how I feel about you, right?

18:00.895 --> 18:02.829
Tell me anyway.

18:03.998 --> 18:05.898
Oh, okay.

18:06.067 --> 18:09.594
Well, as you know,
we've had our ups and downs.

18:09.771 --> 18:12.604
I told you that was my medication.

18:13.975 --> 18:17.138
- I was talking about our relationship.
- Oh, yes.

18:17.312 --> 18:19.337
That's had ups and downs too.

18:19.514 --> 18:21.175
Continue.

18:21.349 --> 18:24.580
Well, uh, I'm thinking
we're not getting any younger.

18:24.752 --> 18:27.653
You know, there was a time when
I did think I was getting younger...

18:27.822 --> 18:30.655
...but it turns out that
that was my medication.

18:31.259 --> 18:34.786
- Sure.
- I also thought I was getting smaller.

18:36.898 --> 18:38.559
Ah. Ahem.

18:39.234 --> 18:43.762
Anyway, uh, it struck me that-
That life is short...

18:43.938 --> 18:48.102
...and maybe the time has come for you
and I to start thinking about our future.

18:49.177 --> 18:50.201
What about it?

18:51.646 --> 18:53.614
Aah, well...

18:54.249 --> 18:57.480
...I know this is kind of sudden, but-

19:04.792 --> 19:05.816
Rose?

19:06.361 --> 19:07.487
Yes, Charlie?

19:08.029 --> 19:09.690
Would you do me the honor of-?

19:13.601 --> 19:16.934
I'm sorry, let me just get rid of this.

19:17.205 --> 19:18.832
Oh, it's my doctor.

19:21.242 --> 19:23.506
Hey, doc, what's the word?

19:24.746 --> 19:26.077
No liver damage whatsoever?

19:30.051 --> 19:31.746
What about my heart?

19:32.654 --> 19:34.679
Well, that's terrific.

19:34.856 --> 19:36.824
Lungs are good too?

19:37.592 --> 19:40.060
So I don't have to give up cigars?

19:40.461 --> 19:42.156
No, no. No, I won't overdo it.

19:42.330 --> 19:44.025
Just when I drink, heh, heh.

19:46.134 --> 19:49.069
Speaking of which, how's the plumbing?

19:49.337 --> 19:51.430
Does that include the prostate?

19:51.606 --> 19:53.437
Yes.

19:55.610 --> 19:59.046
All right, well, uh,
thanks for getting back to me so soon.

19:59.213 --> 20:02.080
And again, I'm- I'm- I'm sorry
for all the name-calling...

20:02.250 --> 20:04.946
...when you slipped your finger up there.

20:14.495 --> 20:16.292
Oh, boy, this is awkward.

20:26.474 --> 20:27.668
Look at him.

20:27.842 --> 20:29.867
He's gonna live forever.

20:30.044 --> 20:33.673
No, it's just gonna seem like forever.

20:35.450 --> 20:39.784
He smokes, he drinks,
parties like there's no tomorrow.

20:39.954 --> 20:42.548
Me? I have Mexican food
and a couple of beers...

20:42.724 --> 20:44.692
...and I'm farting blood.

20:46.995 --> 20:49.293
Yeah. Boo-hoo.

20:49.464 --> 20:53.298
You just said "Mexican food"
and I grew a third butt cheek.

20:54.068 --> 20:55.558
Life isn't fair, is it, Berta?

20:55.837 --> 20:59.364
If it were, you'd be cleaning my toilets
and I'd have my own talk show.

21:01.209 --> 21:04.201
- A talk show?
- Why not? I'm personable.

21:06.748 --> 21:09.546
At least, he has a clean bill of health.
I'm happy for that.

21:09.717 --> 21:12.811
Me too.
I don't care if I never inherit this house.

21:13.655 --> 21:15.589
Uh, uh, excuse me?

21:15.757 --> 21:17.884
Oh, you ain't seen his new will, huh?

21:18.059 --> 21:20.459
- Ah, what new will?
- Never mind.

21:22.430 --> 21:24.091
But in case tragedy strikes...

21:24.265 --> 21:27.257
...be prepared to clear your crap
out of here in 48 hours.

21:30.738 --> 21:33.002
Son of a bitch.
